# Git, PR, review, merge (generic)
## Git
- Follow the repo's architecture, neighbouring code and its `.cursor/rules` / `AGENTS.md`.
- Minimal diff, implement to acceptance criteria. No libraries "just in case", no refactoring of neighbouring layers unless asked.
- Leave shared clones clean (default branch, no uncommitted changes).
- Never push to the default branch, never force-push; history rewrite only with owner approval.
## Branch naming
- Template: `type/NN-short-english-slug`.
- ASCII lowercase English only (no Cyrillic, no spaces).
- `NN` is the GitHub issue number as its own slash segment (required for issue↔branch matching).
- `type` is one of: `feature` | `fix` | `docs` | `infra` | `chore` | `deps` (map from Russian issue types: разработка→feature, исправление→fix, документация→docs, инфраструктура→infra, зависимости→deps, аналитика/тесты/процесс→chore or docs as fits).
- `short-english-slug`: 2–5 kebab-case words describing the change.
- Examples: `feature/101-client-profile-ui`, `fix/218-refresh-token-security`, `docs/303-issue-templates`, `infra/318-actions-english-names`.
- Dependabot keeps GitHub/Dependabot default branch names (do not rename).
- Create via: `gh issue develop <NN> --name type/NN-short-english-slug --base main`.
- Deprecated: role prefixes like `lead/`, `cursor/`, `developer/` and Russian prefixes like `разработка/`. Replace with `type/` above. Prefer deleting old junk branches over renaming them.
- After merge: head branches must auto-delete via the GitHub repo setting «Automatically delete head branches». If that setting is off, ask the owner to turn it on. Agents do not hand-delete after every merge as the primary path; orphans still get cleaned in the weekly audit.
## Tasks and PRs
- One issue = one owner = one PR (batch small related fixes). Status lives in the tracker (labels, board, review state), not in chat.
- **Issue ↔ branch during work; closedBy after close (unless Dependabot):** branch `type/NN-short-english-slug` via `gh issue develop <NN> --name type/NN-short-english-slug --base main` (`linkedBranches`). PR body `## Задача` with `#NN` only, never `closes`/`fix`/`fixes`. Do not call `addCloseIssueReferences` and do not attach closedBy before acceptance. If the branch already exists, do not add or remove Development links by hand. Before merge, the close workflow must be able to match the PR (branch segment and/or `#NN` in the title or body; a closing keyword is not required) and «Задача» must be `#NN`. Do not create closedBy to pass the gate. After the issue is closed, `.github/workflows/link-closed-by.yml` sets the Projects PR chip. Agents do not add or remove Development links unless the owner explicitly asks. Dependabot: no issue link. Docs/process-only meta with no tracker task: «без задачи» (rare). Do not retrofit old closed issues. Details: `project-github-formats.mdc`.
- Post to chat only the PR link when ready, a blocker, or a decision question.
- Behaviour, API, contract, settings, or infra change: the PR names the `Doc-` page to write after merge, or «вики не затронута». The wiki text is written after the change is in `main` (`playbook-step-08-docs.mdc`). Merge does not wait for that wiki edit, and the wiki page is not updated before `main`.
## Review and CI
- CI is the gate: do not re-run locally what CI runs green; read failures from the job log, quote only failing lines.
- Review the diff, not the repo; comment only on problems.
- Depth by risk: trivial (docs, typos, trivial config) = CI + first-line review; normal code = CI + first-line review; risky (infra, CI, Docker/nginx, auth, data/migrations, secrets handling, runtime/network dependencies) = CI + first-line review + deeper security check.
- When the project enables Cursor Automations (`project-cursor-automations.mdc`), those comments are the first-line review; do not duplicate the same checklist in a second pass. Reading every finding and replying on its thread is required; that reply is not a second checklist pass. Escalation rules live in `playbook-step-06-review.mdc`.
## Merge and deploy
- Merge only when all gates are met; only the designated merger merges. Before merge: branch link or a match the close workflow can use, and «Задача» is `#NN` (unless Dependabot / «без задачи»); do not require a closedBy chip while the issue is still open. CI and Cursor Automations have finished (do not merge while a run is in progress); every open finding has a finished reply (`playbook-step-06-review.mdc`). Do not squash-merge while a finding has no reply, or while the reply only promises a fix.
- If the owner already put the task in work or explicitly authorized that work, and the PR matches that scope, merge without a separate yes and notify the owner after merge. Ask before merge only for the cases in `00-core.mdc`.
- Merge = deploy: one PR at a time; next merge only after the previous deploy is green.
- After merge that needs acceptance on dev: before yielding, set `Waiting on` = Deploy in the lead pipeline note; the durable «TravelAgency CI/CD» webhook (Notify orchestrator) unblocks Приёмка (`playbook-workflow.mdc`). No per-task wait-watch and no arm-then-check.
- Dependencies (Dependabot), same split as `00-core.mdc`: for npm and NuGet only (minor, patch, and major; majors are separate PRs, groups are minor/patch only), squash-merge without a separate owner yes when CI is green and nothing needs the owner's clarification. Treat a peer conflict, red CI, or an unclear breaking change as needing clarification. After every such merge, notify the owner what was merged. When something needs a decision or a coordinated fix, do not merge: notify the owner or follow the fix path. docker and github-actions (including grouped updates that may contain majors) still need owner «да» before merge: merge deploys to dev with SSH secrets, and CI does not validate image or action supply chain the way app build and tests do.
- Open PR hygiene (lead): no open PR without an owner and a next step; ask the same day if blocked.
## Testing
- Locally: only tests for the touched area. After deploy: affected flows vs criteria + short smoke. Full regression only before a release or after wide changes (auth, routing, migrations).
## Servers
- Read logs/status freely. Any change, manual deploy or rollback: owner approval, back up configs first.
## Stop rule
- On «стоп»: finish or revert the current atomic step, leave clones clean, push nothing half-done, report branch/PR state, start nothing new.
